When it becomes too difficult to move shrubs apart with your hands, you take a long hand-made machete, which comic book heroes sometimes have, out of your backpack. You made the machete with your dad, just for fun. Your father grumbled all the time, that such a knife is not a toy for kids. Probably, now he would be glad for you. You fancy yourself as an adventurer, who goes through the jungle for a treasure. Your make a good progress, and soon you see the lake through gaps between bushes, the lake that you are heading for.
Finally, last bushes fall under your pressure, and with a sense of relief you step on the oozy shore of the lake, leaving thick shrubberies behind.